	(text "DO-160G protection. ASSUMED Section 22 pin injection LEVEL 3 -\nnot specified, so it is stated here rather than implied. Level 4\nor 5 need larger clamps and more series impedance than these.\n\nOrder is deliberate: series L, then clamp, then ORing, then bulk.\nA TVS with no series impedance ahead of it absorbs the whole\ninjected energy itself, which is how a correctly chosen part\nstill fails.\n\nSECTION 16 POWER INTERRUPT IS NOT MET. Three cards at 1.2 A\nriding 5.16 V down to 4.50 V need 364 mF for 200 ms - a\nsupercapacitor bank, not a capacitor. C60 is sized for the\nfeed-to-feed switchover it CAN cover, about 1 ms. Holding up\nlonger means doing it at a higher voltage ahead of the ORing, or\nrequiring the airframe to provide it."
		(at 29.21 13.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc814f98-7273-48cb-ac9b-7a2f2ca6a501")
	)
